{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMjEcTMCWzXm1KCq1yvn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `roles_repo` config key. Role directories from the shared repo, pinned by ref, are merged into the config snapshot, and a local directory of the same kind and name wins whole. `go test ./...` passes, including new tests for config validation, `SharedRoles` and the shared-repo flow. `make lint` did not finish within the tool timeout, so I only ran `go vet` on the changed packages, which is clean.\n\n- **Pinning:** `roles_repo` takes `repo` and `ref`, validated like sidecars, with `ref` defaulting to `main`. If the shared repo can't be fetched or a shared role is invalid, the config fails to load and nothing is published.\n- **Moving refs:** if a branch or tag in the shared repo moves while the local commit is unchanged, a new snapshot is exported, named `<sha>+<shared12>`.\n- **Wiring:** the shared repo is cached under `~/.ard/roles-repo/<owner>/<repo>`, set up in `internal/servecmd/serve.go`.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` documents the key and recommends pinning a full commit SHA, since a branch or tag can change roles without a PR here.\n- **Not done:** `ard config check` shows `roles_repo` but not which roles came from the shared repo (`Role.Shared` in the plan). I skipped it to keep the diff small.\n- **Not done:** turning `roles_repo` on in this repo's own `.ard/config.yaml` is a protected-path change and needs a human.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/59/worker-engineer.md`. The new tests are in `internal/configsrc/shared_test.go`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":932,"cache_read_input_tokens":55457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":932},"output_tokens":551,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[